      "tier": "core",
      "quote": "all alarms must have actions disabled",
      "quantifier": "all"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The prompt states the three names, and a template can give them as AlarmName or as the logical ID (the ground truth uses only logical IDs), so the name checks accept either; the logical-ID branch is used only because the prompt states these exact names. Each name check also binds the name to its TreatMissingData value ('respectively'). Names are detail because the scenario's point is the TreatMissingData behaviour, whose values are core. Metric identity is core and the evaluation settings are detail. ActionsEnabled defaults to true in CloudFormation, so omitting it correctly fails actions_disabled."
